       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose, the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. Overdoses of this size have also caused non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and the effects can last a long time because amlodipine has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n\nIf 50 mg is what you want, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
